        'A 2022 meta-analysis by Gan and colleagues looked at 14 studies of the body scan practiced on its own. Compared with passive controls, it produced only a small increase in mindfulness, and the authors concluded that the body scan alone is not effective enough to improve health-related outcomes. Study quality was low and results varied a lot. So think of the body scan not as a miracle relaxation technique but as one part of a wider meditation routine.',
