      example: { title: 'Mehmet, 58, retired teacher', text: 'Mehmet found watching his breath made him fidgety, so he tried Benson’s method after his afternoon tea. He chose a short phrase of remembrance from his prayers, one he had known since childhood. He sat in his armchair, relaxed his muscles from his feet up to his face, and silently said the phrase on each out-breath. Thoughts about his grandson’s exam kept arriving. Each time he said to himself “that’s all right” and went back to the phrase, at the same slow pace. After ten minutes he sat quietly for another minute before getting up. He did not feel transformed. He did notice he had not looked at his phone for eleven minutes, which was new. He decided to keep the same phrase and the same armchair for the rest of the week.' },
